1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,080
Once upon a time, there was a man who died.

2
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:11,900
The last story the man was writing was about a brave and handsome prince

3
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:14,840
who vanquishes a crafty raven.

4
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:21,900
When the man died, the raven and the prince escaped from within the story.

5
00:00:22,940 --> 00:00:27,820
The prince took out his own heart to seal away the raven.

6
00:00:27,820 --> 00:00:34,240
But this power, which had been granted solely to him, was nevertheless forbidden.

7
00:00:36,080 --> 00:00:39,600
Thus sealed, the raven troubled them no more.

8
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:45,980
But the prince's heart was shattered and the shards scattered all over town.

9
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:51,980
Ever since then, stories and reality have intermingled in the town,

10
00:00:51,980 --> 00:00:57,180
making it a world where the fantastical was no longer fantastical.

11
00:00:58,660 --> 00:01:01,240
The andes

12
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:01,460
pensar

13
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:02,960
The

14
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:03,960
Andes

15
00:01:03,960 --> 00:01:05,160
The

16
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:11,640
The

17
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:51,600
A dream? Where am I?

18
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:55,600
What am I doing here?

19
00:02:55,600 --> 00:02:57,600
Quack!

20
00:02:57,600 --> 00:02:59,600
Huh? What?

21
00:02:59,600 --> 00:03:03,600
No way, no way, no way, no way, no way, no way, no way!

22
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:09,600
Quack. I'm just a duck.

23
00:03:09,600 --> 00:03:12,600
And I thought I was a girl.

24
00:03:12,600 --> 00:03:15,600
When I saved Senior Muto, was that a dream?

25
00:03:15,600 --> 00:03:18,600
Quack, could this be a dream right now?

26
00:03:18,600 --> 00:03:23,600
If you must know, neither is a dream, little duck.

27
00:03:27,600 --> 00:03:29,600
How are you?

28
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:32,600
You may address me as Strasselmeyer.

29
00:03:34,600 --> 00:03:38,600
Do you still want to save the poor prince who's lost his heart?

30
00:03:38,600 --> 00:03:41,600
The person I want to save is Senior Muto.

31
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:44,600
The prince was a wholehearted hero who fought the demonic raven.

32
00:03:44,600 --> 00:03:47,600
Well, he was when they were still inside the story.

33
00:03:47,600 --> 00:03:49,600
Inside the story?

34
00:03:49,600 --> 00:03:56,600
Yes. He came out of the story, I wrote, and ended up losing his heart to seal the raven away.

35
00:03:56,600 --> 00:04:00,600
Shattered to pieces, his lost heart now wanders as a handful of shards.

36
00:04:00,600 --> 00:04:03,600
And Princess Tutu is the only one who can restore his heart.

37
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:06,600
Princess... Tutu?

38
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:11,600
If you have the necessary resolve, I'll turn you into a girl once more.

39
00:04:11,600 --> 00:04:15,600
A girl? I'll really get to see Senior Muto again?

40
00:04:15,600 --> 00:04:17,600
If you have the resolve, that is?

41
00:04:17,600 --> 00:04:19,600
I do! I do!

42
00:04:19,600 --> 00:04:29,600
If I could be a girl again and stay by Senior Muto's side, maybe someday, someday I might be able to put a smile back on his face.

43
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:34,600
And if that's the one thing I can do, then there's nothing more that I could wish for.

44
00:04:34,600 --> 00:04:57,600
Congratulations, dream, and your wish is granted. That's the great thing about stories. The duck will become a girl, and the girl will become Princess Tutu. Stories are such wonderful creatures. But remember this, if you say or do anything resembling a duck...

45
00:04:57,600 --> 00:04:59,600
What?

46
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:01,600
You just remember that.

47
00:05:14,600 --> 00:05:23,600
This is Gold Crown Town, and I'm...

48
00:05:23,600 --> 00:05:25,600
Quack! A duck!

49
00:05:25,600 --> 00:05:28,600
Quack, quack, quack, quack, quack, quack, quack, quack, quack, quack!

50
00:05:28,600 --> 00:05:30,600
I am a duck.

51
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:35,600
So, Senior Muto and the Prince were all a dream.

52
00:05:35,600 --> 00:05:37,600
Of course.

53
00:05:37,600 --> 00:05:40,600
It's so calming to be on the water.

54
00:05:40,600 --> 00:05:42,600
Quack!

55
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:48,600
Quack!

56
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:52,600
If you say or do anything resembling a duck...

57
00:05:52,600 --> 00:05:54,600
Oh, this is...

58
00:05:54,600 --> 00:05:56,600
It wasn't a dream.

59
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:00,600
Huh?

60
00:06:10,600 --> 00:06:14,600
May those who accept their fate be granted happiness.

61
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:17,600
May those who defy it be granted glory.

62
00:06:17,600 --> 00:06:19,600
Who's that?

63
00:06:19,600 --> 00:06:21,600
I am Adel.

64
00:06:21,600 --> 00:06:23,600
You are a duck.

65
00:06:23,600 --> 00:06:24,600
You know about me?

66
00:06:24,600 --> 00:06:29,600
Even as a girl, you still have some duck-like qualities about you, don't you?

67
00:06:29,600 --> 00:06:30,600
What?

68
00:06:30,600 --> 00:06:31,600
The way you look.

69
00:06:31,600 --> 00:06:32,600
The way I look?

70
00:06:32,600 --> 00:06:35,600
Think of it as having had all your feathers plucked out.

71
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:36,600
These are for you.

72
00:06:36,600 --> 00:06:49,600
So, if I am a duck as in the bird, since when was the girl me, the me that I am?

73
00:06:49,600 --> 00:06:54,600
Or rather, yesterday me and two days ago me, and the me before that are all me, so...

74
00:06:54,600 --> 00:06:55,600
Great!

75
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:57,600
Now I'm really lost!

76
00:06:57,600 --> 00:06:59,600
A story's birth is a sudden event.

77
00:06:59,600 --> 00:07:01,600
The start, a happy accident.

78
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:04,600
The end, the fate for which it's meant.

79
00:07:04,600 --> 00:07:07,600
A story that never ends is a cruel thing.

80
00:07:07,600 --> 00:07:11,600
I'm afraid you lost me too, Miss Adel.

81
00:07:11,600 --> 00:07:12,600
Let us meet again.

82
00:07:12,600 --> 00:07:13,600
Yes.

83
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:23,600
Oh well, oh well, oh well, oh well.

84
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:25,920
You're not partir!

85
00:07:28,060 --> 00:07:30,400
Overall, Mathで both arms

86
00:07:32,320 --> 00:07:34,260
Manuel!

87
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,180
Senior Meworu.

88
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:44,100
I turned into Princess Tutu

89
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:46,500
and saved Senior Meworu, right?

90
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:49,980
I wonder if he remembers.

91
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:52,900
Even if he did, he wouldn't people know, it was me.

92
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:57,740
Oh, what if he found out I was a duck, like the actual bird?

93
00:07:57,960 --> 00:08:01,760
A duck? You're the worst. No wonder you talk like a duck. Shoo, shoo.

94
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:04,680
